From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:51:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: Decode a UTF8String into the room it was sized for.

The terminating null went at twice the string's length, past what the
size pass made room for, and the length allowed was a byte count less
the size of a CERT_NAME_VALUE, which goes negative.  PKIFreeText, the
text of a time stamp response, is UTF8Strings decoded by this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/decode.c b/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
index c0db949ed47..72036a2c724 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
@@ -2623,7 +2623,7 @@ static BOOL CRYPT_AsnDecodeUnicodeString(const BYTE *pbEncoded,
                 {
                     int len = MultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8, 0,
                      (LPCSTR)pbEncoded + 1 + lenBytes, dataLen,
-                     str, bytesNeeded - sizeof(CERT_NAME_VALUE)) * 2;
+                     str, (bytesNeeded - sizeof(LPWSTR)) / sizeof(WCHAR));
                     str[len] = 0;
                     break;
                 }
